  "deviations": [
    {
      "policy": "A2",
      "what": "Dockerfile: `RUN wget -O $SRC/seeds.zip '<url>'` after the samba clone, same URL samba's lib/fuzzing/oss-fuzz/do_build.sh fetches (https://gitlab.com/samba-team/samba-fuzz-seeds/-/jobs/artifacts/master/download?job=zips). ossfuzz/build.sh: before the exec, one guarded sed on lib/fuzzing/oss-fuzz/do_build.sh replaces only its two-line `wget <url> \\ -O seeds.zip` command with `cp $SRC/seeds.zip seeds.zip`; all other lines of the glue are byte-identical, and the seeds are unpacked by the unchanged `$PYTHON -mzipfile -e seeds.zip $OUT` line.",
      "why": "compile runs with --network none; the compile-time wget of the seed zip was the only fatal step (gitlab.com unresolvable, compile exited 4) after every harness had been built.",
      "affects_measurement": false,
      "rationale": "Ruling R4: do_build.sh/build_samba.sh is OSS-Fuzz build glue living in the samba repo. Same seed archive from the same URL, fetched at image-build time instead of compile time; no compile flags, harnesses or project source change."
    },
    {
      "policy": "A2",
      "what": "Dockerfile seed pre-fetch (previous deviation) uses `wget --no-iri`.",
      "why": "Round 1 image build: the pre-fetch got HTTP 403 from cdn.artifacts.gitlab-static.net. With LANG unset in the base image, wget's IRI processing rewrites the signed redirect URL (%2A%27%27 -> *''), which invalidates the signature. --no-iri (or a UTF-8 locale, or curl) fetches it.",
      "affects_measurement": false,
      "rationale": "Part of the A2 move: transport flag only, same URL; the archive is byte-identical to the one fetched from the host (sha256 16fd9ed66e8bb30222c3faf0db397a8365f22e06382fea6539d94c36376715fc, 16145198 bytes)."
    },
    {
      "what": "Built with FUZZING_ENGINE=afl although samba's project.yaml lists only libfuzzer and honggfuzz (controller ruling R10)",
      "why": "The pipeline fuzzes every target with AFL++; samba is the only onboarded project whose OSS-Fuzz config excludes afl. The build goes through OSS-Fuzz's standard compile/compile_afl path unchanged.",
      "affects_measurement": true,
      "rationale": "OSS-Fuzz never produces an AFL++ build of samba, so 'as OSS-Fuzz would build it' does not hold for the engine; the address-sanitizer build and the harnesses are OSS-Fuzz's. The undefined build fails at a host tool link (recoverable __ubsan_handle_*_overflow handlers unresolved through afl-clang-fast++): recorded compile_failed, one fix round per policy, not pursued. samba is a spare with address only."
    }
  ]
